ing to  not be hurt by this except for you know  the most privileged wealthy elite group  of white men I think even you know  there's this sort of myth of the Trump  voter as a struggling working-class  white man I don't think that myth is  really borne out and voting data you  know they're definitely white people but  of all different classes but I think  they will be heard as well you know the  folks in Missouri where I live who voted  for him I think well already you know  they will be hurt like what he did with  Boeing yesterday which is a big provider  of employment in st. Louis  you know it's potentially very harmful  for folks who may have voted for him so  basically you know we're all in trouble  when the president's main interest is  himself and he's devoid of conscience  and his administration is as well and is  you know flipping almost in their  treatment of marginalized and vulnerable  people then we're in deep trouble as a  country so our last thing I want to  touch on and next week we're going to  have a former neo-nazi to comment on  this with regard to the anti-semitism  aspect of everything that that's been  going on you know we've seen this  support of Trump from of white  nationalists former  kkkv like we've not seen for a  presidential candidate in a very long  time why do you think they're giving him  a pass on the reality that he has a  Jewish daughter a Jewish son-in-law that  clearly is a very close and trusted  adviser Jewish grandchildren in how are  how are these individuals rationalizing  that away in their support for Trump I  mean I think that they see Trump is the  key to a bigger goal and so they're  willing to overlook that  especially since Jared Kushner is a key  player in bringing the school for it as  it's Sheldon Adelson and other Jewish  backers of Trump you know I think it's  it's really unfortunate you can just  judge a person by their actions and not  their affinities and when Jewish  journalists and Jewish citizens are  being attacked then there's a moral  obligation to speak up against that so I  don't think it's good enough to say Oh  Trump can't be anti-semitic or his team  can't be anti-semitic because he happens  to have you know a Jewish son-in-law and  a daughter who converted to Judaism  they're not doing anything as Jews to  stop these sorts of attacks on fellow  Jews and I think that that is you know  what you should look at and judge  because just like Trump they could be  doing a lot to stop this to stop this  kind of hateful rhetoric to denounce  groups like the Ku Klux Klan and you  know to denounce other anti-semitic  groups and they're not doing it so it  just shows it's not a priority for them  and I think that's very unfortunate  we've been speaking with Sarah Kenzie or  we started talking about her article our  fate was sealed long before November 8th  but she's written more since then as  well and I encourage you to check out  her work Sarah thanks so much for  joining me today thank you thank you for  having me

